Incremental Search
Finds the expression which you start typing. Plant Simulation highlights the character combination while
you type in the text window.
Description
Microsoft describes Incremental Search as "a type of search that looks for a string in an automatic and
progressive way. As the user types a string, possible matches are found, thus enabling the user to stop
typing the complete string as soon as the right match is found."
• If you mistype a word, delete the last character you typed by pressing Backspace. Then, type in the
correct character.
• Press F3 to find the next instance of the expression.
• Press Esc to terminate Incremental Search.
Incremental Search for Workers
Incremental Search also finds Workers, which are located on Workplaces, FootPaths, and on their way to
the WorkerPool. It does not find Workers located in the WorkerPool though.
In general, Incremental Search finds objects by their name. For Workers Incremental Search also
includes the name of the class and the counter of the instance. For Worker:1 Incremental Search
finds the first instance of the class named Worker for example.
Incremental Search
