Auto Complete
Auto Complete is an automatic data entry mechanism: Type in the first letter or letters the name of
an attribute/read-only attribute/method, and press Ctrl+Spacebar or Shift+Ctrl+Spacebar or click Auto
Complete.
Remarks
When Plant Simulation reaches a point at which the name is not unique anymore, it opens a window
in which you can select an attribute/read-only attribute/method. Move the cursor over the name of the
attribute/read-only attribute/method of your choice and double-click to select it or use the up and down
keys on your keyboard to move within the list. Press the Enter key to select the entry of your choice.
Plant Simulation then automatically completes the name for you and adds the corresponding characters
—period, opening parenthesis, assignment operator (:=), and closing parenthesis to your source code if
necessary.
You can filter the attribute/read-only attribute/method, which the object provides, according to the same
criteria as in the window Show Attributes and Methods. To make the window larger, drag the mouse over
one of the sides or a corner of the window and drag the mouse.
Auto Complete
Plant Simulation Help 11-3607
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

To do this Click
Show Attributes/Methods for Standard Users
Show Attributes/Methods for Expert Users
Show General Attributes/Methods
Show User Interface/Animation Attributes/Methods
Show Control Attributes/Methods
Show Simulation Attributes/Methods
Show Energy related Attributes/Methods
Show 3D Attributes and Methods
Show Statistics Attributes/Methods
Show Attributes. This encompasses the built-in attributes, local
variables, and objects of type Variable.
Show Read-Only Attributes. These are attributes and methods, which
do not expect parameters, which do not have side effects, and which
return a value.
Show Methods. Methods as a rule have parameters, have side effects,
and return a value. The command shows the built-in methods, user-
defined attributes of type method, and objects of type Variable.
Show Global Functions. This encompasses global functions and
constants.
Show Objects. This encompasses objects in the Frame, objects of type
Variable and objects of type Method.
Show Keywords
If you insert a function or a Method with parameters into a Method, Plant Simulation shows the status bar.
The status bar shows the signature of the function/Method and thus makes typing the required parameters
in easier. Plant Simulation hides the status bar again when you type in the closing parenthesis or when
you press Esc.
Auto Complete
