SimTalk
setErrorHandler [SimTalk]
Select Template
Plant Simulation Help 11-3617
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Create Your Own Method Templates
Create a method template of your own in a text editor and save it as a text file (*.txt).
Remarks
The syntax for creating your own method template is quite simple:
• Create the file in the subfolder C:\Program Files\Siemens\Plant Simulation
XX\Templates\English\Name_of_Your_Category. The dialog Select Template shows this name in the
field below Select the Category.
• Type in two hyphens -- followed by the key combination which you want to use if you want to set a key
combination.
• Type in two hyphens -- and the name of the template. The dialog Select Template shows this name in
the field below Select the Template.
• Type in two hyphens -- and a description of the template. The dialog Select Template shows this
description in the rightmost field.
• Type in /* and then the comment which the template itself shows after you loaded it into the Method
Editor. Close this comment with */.
Type in the variable you want to use and any comment you would like to add.
Type in the item you want the user to replace in the source code within left and right pointing double
angle quotation marks, «attribute»=«value» in our example.
If the user drags the mouse over this item, the Method shows the text you type in at the end of the file
as a Tooltip: Start this tooltip text with /* followed by the search term you typed in in the double angle
quotation marks. Finish it with §§*/. You can type in the Tooltip, but do not have to do it.
• Type in the key combination that the user can type in to insert the code snippet.
Proceed as follows to insert the code snippet: Suppose that the key combination is Ctrl+T C. Hold down
Ctrl and press T on the keyboard. Then release Ctrl and type in the letter that is assigned to the code
snippet, C in our case.
The text for the Processing Time depending on an attribute of the part looks like this.
-- Determines the processing time of a station in a formula
-- according to an attribute of the MU.
-- @ is the MU that triggers the formula
-- ? is the station calling this method
->time
if @.«attribute»=«value» 
   result:=«time»
   -- add your code here
elseif @.«attribute»=«value»
   result:=«time»
   -- add your code here
Create Your Own Method Templates
11-3618 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

else
   -- add your code here
end
The Method shows it like this after loading it.
Note
Compare any of the method templates that are part of your program package.
