Toggle Class Breakpoint
Adds or deletes a breakpoint to all instances sharing the source code of this class.
Remarks
Click in the line in which you would like to set a class breakpoint. Then, click Toggle Class Breakpoint or
press F9 to set a class breakpoint in front of the statement of the line of code.
A class breakpoint is designated by a filled red circle 
 .
If you insert a class breakpoint and an instance breakpoint in the same line, the Method shows a white star
within a red circle 
 .
Once the Method reaches a breakpoint while being executed, the Method Debugger opens and highlights
the line in yellow. You can then inspect and modify the contents of the local variables and the parameters.
Instead, you can also:
• Click in the line in which you would like to set a class breakpoint with the right mouse button and select
the command Class Breakpoint in the Context Menu of the Method Debugger.
• Click 
  on the Toolbar of the Method Debugger.
• Click in the area of the row markers and breakpoints.
To activate all breakpoints contained in a line of source code, hold down Ctrl and double-click a
breakpoint.
To open the dialog Breakpoint Settings, hold down Shift and Ctrl and double-click a breakpoint.
If a line of source code contains an Instance Breakpoint and a Class Breakpoint, Plant Simulation opens
the dialog Breakpoint Settings of the Class Breakpoint.
Plant Simulation marks temporary breakpoints in the source code of a Method in a brighter color than
saved breakpoints. This might, for example, be the case if you changed the source code of a Method and
set a breakpoint after the original end of the source code. These breakpoints will be lost if you do not apply
the source code.
You can also set a Class Breakpoint and/or an Instance Breakpoint for an encrypted method. The Method
then stops during method execution in the Method Debugger.
Toggle Class Breakpoint
11-3642 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

If you did set a breakpoint, the Method shows the breakpoint within the Method Editor or the Method
Debugger to the left of the message Source code is encrypted.
