Toggle Instance Breakpoint
Adds or deletes a breakpoint to this instance of the source code only.
Remarks
Click in the line in which you would like to set an Instance Breakpoint. Then, select the command Toggle
Instance Breakpoint or press Shift+ F9 to set an Instance Breakpoint that only applies to this instance.
An Instance Breakpoint is designated by a red star 
 .
If you insert a Class Breakpoint and an Instance Breakpoint in the same line, the Method shows a white
star within a red circle 
 .
Once the Method reaches this breakpoint while the Method is being executed, Plant Simulation opens the
Method Debugger and displays the line inverted in yellow. You can then inspect and modify the contents
of the local variables and the parameters.
Instead, you can also click in the line in which you would like to set an Instance Breakpoint with the
right mouse button and select the command Instance Breakpoint in the Context Menu of the Method
Debugger.
Plant Simulation shows temporary breakpoints in the source code of a Method in a brighter color than
saved breakpoints. This might, for example, be the case when you changed the source code of a Method
and set a breakpoint after the original end of the source code. These breakpoints will be lost if you do not
apply the source code.
To activate or deactivate Instance Breakpoints, hold down Shift and click in the area of the row markers
and breakpoints.
You can also set a Class Breakpoint and/or an Instance Breakpoint for an encrypted method. The Method
then stops during method execution in the Method Debugger.
If you did set a breakpoint, the Method shows the breakpoint within the Method Editor or the Method
Debugger to the left of the message Source code is encrypted.
See also
Working with Breakpoints
