New Syntax [command]
Activates SimTalk 2.0 syntax.
Remarks
Then you have to type the source code into Methods in the improved, abbreviated notation.
If you want to use SimTalk 2.0 syntax for all new Methods which you are going to program, activate New
Syntax in the Method class in the Class Library.
Note
Clicking New Syntax for an existing Method, whose source code you created in SimTalk 1.0 notation,
automatically converts that source code to source code in the correct SimTalk 2.0 notation.
Plant Simulation writes the setting New Syntax to the model file.
If New Syntax is deactivated, you have to type the source code into Methods using SimTalk 1.0 notation.
To convert the source code of all existing Methods in a simulation model to the new syntax, hold down
Shift, click the object Basis in the Class Library with the right mouse button and click Convert all Methods
to New Syntax.
New Syntax [command]
