Syntax-controlled Indentation [Tools ribbon]
Activates or deactivates the indentation of the source code you type in according to the predefined SimTalk
syntax.
Remarks
If Syntax-controlled Indentation is active, Plant Simulation automatically indents the cursor when
starting a new line of code according to the delimiting keywords. Plant Simulation indents, for example,
the text between if and end, making it easier to follow the logic behind the source code.
The Method Editor aligns the source code with the previous line of code.
If you change this setting, the change applies during the entire Plant Simulation session for all newly
opened Methods.
Note
The command Syntax-controlled Indentation is not available in SimTalk Version 1.0.
Syntax-controlled Indentation [Tools ribbon]
Plant Simulation Help 11-3661
